WEBVTT

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.840
The false peace
has been shattered.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.210
A remnant force
claiming to be Zeon...

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.210
...has attacked a Federation
test base in Australia.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.550
They have successfully
stolen one mobile suit.

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:18.780
It is the Gundam Unit 2,
armed with a nuclear warhead.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.790
The effects of this incident...

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.730
...will spread to every
corner of the Earth system.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.220
The year is U.C. 0083.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:51.670
Mobile Suit Gundam 0083

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:58.120
shourisha nado inai tatakai ni tsukare hate
There's no winner of this fight as I collapse, now exhausted.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.090
hoshizora o miageru
I look up to the stars above...

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:03.760
naku koto mo kanawanai
...and don't even have the strength to cry.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:09.130
I don't need kinou nado iranai
I don't need, don't need yesterday anymore.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:15.410
I don't need kuchi hateta yume mo
I don't need dreams that have crumbled away.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.640
I got a burning heart!

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.640
mune o tsuranuku suriru wo
I just wanna keep on running!

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:27.480
tada oi kakete hashiri tsuzuketai
Just chasing the thrill that's shooting through my heart!

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.150
kotoba ni dekinai omoi ga
Feelings that you just can't describe with words...

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:40.040
kogoeta kokoro sae atsuku saseru
...are enough to ignite even a frozen heart!

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:43.700
I got a burning love!

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.770
aoku kagayaku honoo de
Burning with shining blue fire.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:51.490
kono hoshizora o ooi tsukusu toki made
Fire that'll spread until it covers all the stars in the sky.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:55.850
I got a burning heart!

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.980
ai wa kodoku na tatakai
Love is such a lonely battle.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:04.790
kono sekai made moyashi tsukusu no ka
But is it one that will consume the world in flames?

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:29.850
ENDLESS PURSUIT

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.110
Who does he think he is?

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.380
Hey, kid.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:53.280
OUT OF MY WAY!

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.530
Hurry up and put out the
fires from the missile hits!

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.510
Haven't you contacted
General Marnery yet?!

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.840
Nina!

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.570
NO! My poor Gundams!

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.040
Ensign Uraki! This is Captain
Synapse on the <i>Albion!</i>

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.050
Leave the recovery of Unit 2
to the other mobile suits...

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.920
...and get back here at once!

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.820
I can't!
I'm already engaging him!

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.560
And I still have
a chance to win!

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.430
<i>I... I can do this!</i>

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.960
He's got the guts,
but he doesn't have the skill!

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.740
<i>Ensign Uraki!</i>

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.520
<i>You aren't ready to</i>
<i>take me on yet!</i>

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.920
<i>Amateur!</i>

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.590
Amateur, huh?!

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:30.140
U-801, your shots are drifting to
the east. Correct your solution.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:31.870
<i>U-801, acknowledged.</i>

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:33.910
Time to join in.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.560
Wh- What was that?!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.560
It wasn't a missile
from the enemy ship!

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.500
You mean they have a heavy
mobile suit out there, too?!

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.900
And another one!

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:04.480
Looks like the commander did it.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.910
Not bad for someone
who just landed here!

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:15.150
Captain!
General Marnery's been killed!

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.890
What? The base's
commander is dead?

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:23.900
Nina...

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.300
First time in combat?
That's right, you aren't a soldier.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:42.820
<i>Ensign Uraki! Ensign Uraki!</i>
<i>What's wrong? Respond!</i>

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.880
<i>Ensign Uraki!</i>

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.580
<i>ENSIGN URAKI!!!</i>

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:50.890
Don't go to pieces
over a missile shower!

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.230
Lieutenant Burning...

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:01.830
<i>The enemy's retreated. We're</i>
<i>going after Unit 2 to recover it.</i>

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:04.570
<i>Take the rifle Keith</i>
<i>has for you. All clear?</i>

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:12.470
Oh, man... A real battle!
Can you believe it, Kou?

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:15.380
Keith...

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:16.820
<i>Let's go, Uraki!</i>

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:18.050
Aye, sir!

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:22.820
<i>Okay, let's earn our paychecks.</i>
<i>I'll take command of this team.</i>

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:25.490
<i>This is Burning!</i>
<i>We're going after them!</i>

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.320
<i>Burning team, the enemy assault...</i>

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.360
<i>...has left us unable to</i>
<i>coordinate your pursuit!</i>

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.890
<i>Establish contact with the</i>
<i>assault carrier </i>Albion<i>! Out!</i>

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:38.140
Nina, where
are you going?! Wait!

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:39.900
She's going after it?

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.580
Captain, I'm tracking a
high-heat source at 4 o'clock!

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:47.170
- A sixth wave?!
- It's not a missile!

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:50.190
Minovsky particle interference
is preventing a positive ID.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:53.850
A Zeon recovery ship...

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:55.480
Inform Burning's team!

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:56.890
Aye, aye!

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.860
This is Komusai DC-14.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:11.460
Commander Gato, do you read?

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:16.140
<i>Barely. We've stolen the nuke,</i>
<i>along with the prototype Gundam.</i>

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:20.080
You've done it again, sir.
Admiral Delaz will be pleased.

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:22.850
<i>Spare me the compliments.</i>
<i>That's for Earthnoids.</i>

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.880
<i>All right, I'll meet you</i>
<i>at the rendezvous point.</i>

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.360
If this operation is successful,
I'll never have to look up...

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.890
...at the night sky
from the ground again.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.160
<i>Commander!</i>

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.790
<i>I've just picked</i>
<i>up enemy mobile suits.</i>

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:44.860
So, they <i>are</i> chasing us. Did they
pick up the Komusai reentering?

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:46.940
Now hear this! Don't let
them beat us there!

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.700
- <i>Aye, sir!</i>
- <i>Aye!</i>

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.390
What a mess this is.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:13.870
You wouldn't think
the war was over.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.530
You're a real busybody, Mora.

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:19.030
I'm going after the prototypes
because it's my job to.

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:22.840
Well, I guess I want look after
someone who's in over their head.

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:25.500
Hm? You mean me?

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:28.780
I mean the ensign in the Gundam.
Strictly as a mechanic, of course.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:31.150
Oh. Of course.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:35.210
My legs are shaking so much.
I thought I had more nerve than this.

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:37.490
You should look
ahead when you drive.

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:44.260
I think you've got plenty of nerve.

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:56.440
Captain Dreiser, it looks like
Commander Gato was successful.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:58.780
Mm. I see.

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:03.110
Aside from the loss of one Dom
Tropen, everything went as planned.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.520
Shall we set sail?

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:07.820
Number One, Commander Gato
would have a backup plan...

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.830
...in case the Komusai
was destroyed.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.620
Hm? Yes, sir...

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:17.790
He wouldn't have sent us out here
just to fire a few missiles.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.400
Fog's getting thick, isn't it?

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.920
Why would they be
after a nuclear warhead?

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:42.080
To put it simply,
they're being sore losers.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:45.650
Watch your step. This area's
full of places for them to hide.

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:49.430
Y- You think they're
around here?! Kou!

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:52.130
I know, but we're committed now.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.600
<i>Y- Yeah, you're right. Right.</i>

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.930
Allen, quit scaring them.

00:09:56.970 --> 00:10:00.570
Keith! Uraki! Just do
it like you always do.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.910
- I won't let them beat you.
- <i>Aye, sir!</i>

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:06.110
All right, we'll split up.
Uraki, you're with me.

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:24.120
All right! All right!

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:27.070
Commander, we'll take off
as soon as you're locked down.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:29.130
The Feddies
are closing in, right?

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:30.140
Pretty much.

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:33.540
And Chief, have a Lt. commander's
uniform for me next time.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:37.170
Either way, you look a lot
better in a Zeon uniform, sir!

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:39.540
Just sit tight in that
cockpit a little longer!

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:42.780
Of course.
It's <i>my</i> mobile suit, after all.

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:47.920
Over there!

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:51.950
<i>Lt. Burning! Lt. Burning! We've</i>
<i>spotted the Zeon recovery ship.</i>

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:59.090
Okay, Uraki, the target's a
booster-equipped Komusai.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:02.160
<i>Aye, sir. They're planning to</i>
<i>blast out into space, right?</i>

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:06.570
Looks that way. You're going to
charge in as Allen fires at them.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:08.840
Leave any other enemies to me.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:12.180
Lieutenant... I'm sorry
about what happened before.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:16.910
It's just... It was like I forgot
everything I was supposed to do.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:20.120
- That's why I'm here.
- Yeah. Right, sir.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:21.920
Exactly why.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:23.920
All right!

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:31.230
Heh, here we go, Keith.
We'll have 'em in one shot.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:36.170
<i>Lieutenant, their escorts have</i>
<i>pulled out. They have, right?!</i>

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.680
That's why they didn't attack.
Just don't get careless.

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:41.350
R- Right, sir...

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:45.810
Huh?

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:56.020
KEITH!

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:04.790
KEITH!

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:06.530
- <i>Uraki!</i>
- Sir?

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:07.870
<i>Head for the Komusai!</i>

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:09.130
B- But!

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:10.140
<i>GO!</i>

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:11.160
Aye!

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:16.170
What the?!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.850
That's the commander's unit!

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:25.550
Get going, Uraki!
I'll hold him here!

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.120
Lieutenant Burning...

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:48.340
He's coming for us...
Forward guns! Toast that sucker!

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:54.410
S- Stop... Stop!

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:02.580
They're going for it...
Come on, stop!

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.440
Empty! The other weapons!

00:13:32.350 --> 00:13:35.050
Got it... I got it?

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:37.080
Lieutenant Burning! Keith!

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:51.060
God damn you! Anavel Gato
hasn't waited three years...

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:55.840
...just to let you unprincipled
fools stand in the way of our ideals!

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.070
Your ideals?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:01.710
Our dream of true freedom
for all Spacenoids!

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:06.020
We will sever the evil hold of the
Earth with our sword of justice!

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:08.750
Freedom? What's he mean?

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:12.350
Gato? The guy from our
textbooks on modern warfare?!

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:15.920
Anavel Gato...
The Nightmare of Solomon!

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:17.360
What did they say?

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.230
This isn't good.

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:22.130
We're in the middle of a battle
and you start giving speeches?!

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:23.840
You're an officer, aren't you?!

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:27.470
If you want to be more than a grunt,
learn to see the big picture!

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:28.910
Y- Yes, sir...

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:32.900
I'm the ENEMY, you idiot!

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:44.160
<i>Commander! Dreiser's moving in</i>
<i>for a pickup! We don't have time!</i>

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.780
<i>Right! Understood!</i>

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:53.660
Without the Federation behind you,
you couldn't do anything!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.970
- I heard that!
- <i>Uraki! 12 o'clock!</i>

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:01.040
- Why, you... You won't escape!
- <i>Uraki, wait!</i>

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.670
I'm okay, sir!
I'm going after them!

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:06.150
Don't be reckless! What can you
do by yourself?! Cool off, now!

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:15.620
Mora, what was that
ensign's name, again?

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:17.750
Ensign Kou Uraki.

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:21.220
Ensign Kou Uraki...

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:26.670
How dare those Zeon
stragglers say that!

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:29.600
Scott, have you
located that Jukon, yet?

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:33.300
We traced those missiles' path.
Kalent team is on its way.

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:35.340
Good.

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:39.840
It's almost dawn. Go to half-watch!
Simone, bring us down!

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:47.490
<i>Kou...</i>
<i>They got Lieutenant Allen.</i>

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:49.350
They got him?

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:52.090
<i>Direct hit with a
<i>bazooka to the body.</i></i>

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:55.190
Dead... He's dead?

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:58.660
<i>C'mon, you two. We still</i>
<i>have a mission. Follow me.</i>

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:00.700
<i>Keith, inventory</i>
<i>our remaining ammo.</i>

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.860
Lieutenant!
What about Lt. Allen's body?

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.630
- <i>Leave it.</i>
- We can't!

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:08.700
<i>Keith, is there any chance</i>
<i>Allen's still alive?</i>

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:12.980
N- No... There's no possibility.
He was killed, sir...

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:14.710
<i>Do you want to see</i>
<i>what's left of his body?</i>

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.050
No, sir!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.710
<i>Then leave Allen's remains</i>
<i>to the recovery team.</i>

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:21.380
Aye, sir...

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:28.620
<i>Allen... Looks like you beat</i>
<i>us all back to the base...</i>

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:37.970
<i>This is Kalent team.</i>
<i>Have reached target area.</i>

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:41.070
<i>Search underway.</i>
<i>Fog is getting thicker.</i>

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:45.440
<i>We believe the enemy may have</i>
<i>exhausted his ammunition.</i>

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:47.640
<i>We can handle this by ourselves!</i>

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.710
I sure as hell don't want that
pervert Burning hogging the glory!

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:01.520
Captain, it looks like a battle.
It's pretty close to the shore.

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:05.360
I wonder if Commander Gato's
going to set a new kill record.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:07.460
Prepare the
recovery vessel at once!

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:08.630
Aye, sir!

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.720
Kalent team! Kalent!

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.310
Respond! What's wrong?!

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:22.470
Lieutenant Burning,
are we the only ones left?

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:23.800
<i>Looks like it.</i>

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:28.370
The coast looks really foggy.
Are we going to be able to spot them?

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:29.810
<i>We have to find them.</i>

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:33.470
And even if we do,
we have to fight Gato, right?!

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:35.090
<i>Keith, be quiet...</i>

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:39.760
Y- Yeah... The guy who was on the
graduation exam in the Academy!

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:41.320
Lieutenant Anavel Gato.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:45.300
Ace pilot of Vice Admiral
Dozle Zabi's space assault corps!

00:17:45.340 --> 00:17:47.140
Which means!

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:49.330
- Ensign Keith!
- <i>Y- Yes, sir...</i>

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:53.290
Get out your maneuvers stick.
Map number 103.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.810
<i>Y- Yes, sir.</i>

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:58.310
We'll be hitting the Slave Coast
soon, where the enemy was headed.

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:01.310
Where do you think they'll
wait for the recovery ship?

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:04.120
Right. Umm...

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:08.630
Here. We could only attack them
from either the left or the right.

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:11.100
They'd only have to defend
themselves from one direction.

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:12.760
- Ensign Uraki!
- <i>Yes, sir?</i>

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:16.070
If we engaged them there,
who would have the advantage?

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:19.270
Yes, sir! Considering the terrain
and the possibility of an ambush...

00:18:19.310 --> 00:18:22.610
...the enemy would have
the overwhelming advantage...

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:24.480
Overwhelming...

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:33.080
Keith, that's not what
Allen would have said.

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:35.920
Do you think the enemy would
retreat to the place...

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:38.750
...even a green Federal Forces
ensign would think of first?

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:39.730
<i>Uraki.</i>

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:40.750
Yes, sir?

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:44.060
<i>The enemy definitely has the</i>
<i>advantage in terms of firepower.</i>

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.760
<i>But what is his objective?</i>

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:50.100
<i>Getting out of here with Unit 2,</i>
<i>which he's just stolen, right?</i>

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:53.370
<i>Gato may not be able to</i>
<i>face us in a stand up fight.</i>

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:57.810
<i>And will lying in wait let</i>
<i>him win with this visibility?</i>

00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:02.770
When will the fog clear?
When will the recovery ship arrive?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:06.080
He must be as
nervous as we are.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:09.580
Considering this situation,
I think they're here.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:12.680
My gut instinct
says the same thing.

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:16.360
<i>But, more than analyzing the enemy,</i>
<i>the main problem is you two.</i>

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:19.030
<i>This battle will be decided</i>
<i>by whether or not...</i>

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:21.590
<i>...you two stop acting like a
<i>couple of screaming amateurs.</i></i>

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:23.370
<i>Who cares how good Gato is?</i>

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.800
<i>Just remember</i>
<i>what he said to you.</i>

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:29.370
You mean, believe in something?

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:31.380
<i>I can't think of a better</i>
<i>way to put this right now...</i>

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:33.740
<i>...but a battle is decided</i>
<i>in an instant!</i>

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:36.380
<i>A moment's hesitation</i>
<i>and you're dead!</i>

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:37.710
Something to believe in...

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:41.950
<i>Uraki. Ensign Kou Uraki, can you</i>
<i>hear me? This is Nina Purpleton.</i>

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:49.090
What do you want?!
We're about to go into battle!

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.160
We can't send Uraki back now!

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:54.570
<i>No, I just... I just</i>
<i>wanted to ask a favor of you.</i>

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:55.730
What?

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:56.760
A favor?

00:19:56.810 --> 00:20:02.070
<i>Take care of Unit 1. And...</i>
<i>And bring back Unit 2, please!</i>

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:04.700
<i>That's...</i>
<i>That's all I wanted to say.</i>

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:07.650
Right. Understood. I promise.

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:42.780
<i>Move in! No one can</i>
<i>hit anything in this fog!</i>

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:45.120
Behind me!

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:48.790
No?

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:53.280
There you are!

00:21:04.710 --> 00:21:06.400
Shit!
This terrain's impossible!

00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:10.910
This is worse than
fighting hand-to-hand!

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:17.450
Keith!

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:38.010
Adamsky!

00:21:38.050 --> 00:21:40.200
<i>Commander Gato,</i>
<i>do you read me?</i>

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:41.800
<i>We can't see what</i>
<i>your situation is.</i>

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:44.570
<i>We're following the light of your</i>
<i>beam saber! Grab on when we arrive!</i>

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:51.750
Commander, I'll hold
them off here! Get going!

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:53.750
But, with just one Xamel!

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:57.660
<i>This pig couldn't get on the</i>
<i>recovery ship anyway! Go!</i>

00:21:57.730 --> 00:21:58.470
Thank you.

00:21:58.510 --> 00:22:00.090
GATO!!!

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:03.460
What?!

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:14.940
Him again?! Twice he's done it
and now he's going for three?!

00:22:16.710 --> 00:22:17.800
Where are you?!

00:22:37.200 --> 00:22:38.700
Why did you steal Unit 2?!

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:41.660
I have nothing
more to say to you!

00:22:41.700 --> 00:22:43.690
Not to a man who doesn't even
know what's he's fighting for!

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:46.730
I'm still a Federation officer!

00:22:46.770 --> 00:22:49.170
Only a real man
should say those words!

00:22:52.610 --> 00:22:53.710
You're finished!

00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:55.410
Like hell!

00:22:57.990 --> 00:23:00.610
The shield! Aim for
Unit 2's cooling system!

00:23:12.070 --> 00:23:13.760
How could I?!

00:23:21.180 --> 00:23:24.740
Mark my words, Ensign!
I swear I'll destroy anyone...

00:23:24.780 --> 00:23:27.650
...who stands in the way
of the resurrection of Zeon!

00:23:38.760 --> 00:23:40.630
Lieutenant Burning!

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:48.070
Lieutenant!

00:23:59.050 --> 00:24:01.020
Keith! Are you okay?

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:03.240
Dammit, my leg's busted.

00:24:03.280 --> 00:24:07.020
Lieutenant! Hang on, sir.
I'll get you down from there.

00:24:07.060 --> 00:24:10.750
Don't sound so sad, kid.
You're gonna make me cry.

00:25:16.200 --> 00:25:21.240
<i>Don't come to me just 'cause you're lonely tonight...</i>

00:25:21.240 --> 00:25:25.870
<i>Lonely's only part of your game...</i>

00:25:26.250 --> 00:25:31.670
<i>As long as you live, you must remember one thing...</i>

00:25:31.670 --> 00:25:36.450
<i>Give and take are one and the same...</i>

00:25:36.450 --> 00:25:39.020
<i>So tell me are you ready?</i>

00:25:39.020 --> 00:25:41.690
<i>Really, really ready?</i>

00:25:41.690 --> 00:25:46.200
<i>I don't want your love for one night!</i>

00:25:46.200 --> 00:25:51.990
<i>'Cause I'm not lookin' for a love affair...</i>

00:25:51.990 --> 00:25:56.850
<i>I need the magic when I hold you near...</i>

00:25:57.190 --> 00:26:02.340
<i>It's more important than a one-night stand...</i>

00:26:02.340 --> 00:26:07.510
<i>I need the magic when I touch your hand!</i>

00:26:07.510 --> 00:26:12.670
<i>I'm not lookin' for a love affair...</i>

00:26:12.670 --> 00:26:17.840
<i>I need the magic when I hold you near!</i>

00:26:17.840 --> 00:26:23.020
<i>It's more important than a one-night stand...</i>

00:26:23.020 --> 00:26:30.470
<i>I need the magic when I touch...touch your hand...</i>

00:26:49.570 --> 00:26:51.570
NEXT EPISODE

00:26:53.640 --> 00:26:56.410
Unit 2, which vanished
into the morning mist.

00:26:56.450 --> 00:26:59.040
Nina, who can offer
no comforting words.

00:26:59.110 --> 00:27:03.070
The wind blowing through the ruined
base casts a pall on Kou's heart.

00:27:03.120 --> 00:27:06.950
And the arrival of new
allies brings a confrontation.

00:27:06.990 --> 00:27:09.360
Who will end up as
the pilot of Unit 1?

00:27:09.400 --> 00:27:14.420
INTO BATTLE, ALBION!
